// Native RKKY interlayer coupling (ext_RKKY): adjacent layers.
// Field convention  B = J / (Msat * dz) * m_partner.
// J = -2e-3 J/m2, Msat = 1e6 A/m, dz = 0.9e-9 m  ->  |B| = 2.22222 T.
// Layer 0 (region 100) is +z, layer 1 (region 101) is +x. Because J < 0, the
// field in region 100 points along -x (partner is region 101), and the field
// in region 101 points along -z (partner is region 100).
SetGridSize(16, 16, 2)
SetCellSize(2e-9, 2e-9, 0.9e-9)
Msat = 1.0e6
defregion(100, layer(0))
defregion(101, layer(1))
ext_RKKY(100, 101, -2e-3)
m.setRegion(100, uniform(0, 0, 1))
m.setRegion(101, uniform(1, 0, 0))
Run(0)
ExpectV("B_rkky adjacent (region 100)", B_rkky.Region(100).Average(), vector(-2.22222, 0, 0), 1e-3)
ExpectV("B_rkky adjacent (region 101)", B_rkky.Region(101).Average(), vector(0, 0, -2.22222), 1e-3)
